[{:db/id "q-324126/field-1/17f7a92ecac965d3850a7da98658af322c6b691d4b3336f622586133c927298d" :answer/id #uuid "cf4d84af-0206-5b97-85de-5b66087d9512" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-324126/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0c6db1ac-aa23-5653-bb27-23b164dee043" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-324126/field-1/17f7a92ecac965d3850a7da98658af322c6b691d4b3336f622586133c927298d" :answer-field/choices ["q-324126/field-1/17f7a92ecac965d3850a7da98658af322c6b691d4b3336f622586133c927298d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-324126/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "1401baf8-7491-5741-a130-40d84c532447" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-324126/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "c68200df-2bfa-5ec3-98b0-a7dc12643e10" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-324126/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-324126/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-324126" :question/id #uuid "a920c85e-6aa9-5e63-8475-d17a64777df2" :question/math-academy-id "q-324126" :question/problem "The values of $x$ that satisfy the inequality $\\frac{11-4x}{3-x}<0$ lie in the interval\n\n$\\,x\\in ($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we define the function $f(x)$ as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{11-4x}{3-x}.\n$$\n\nSo we're now solving the inequality $f(x)<0.$\n\nThe solution to the equation $f(x)=0$ is $x=\\frac{11}{4}.$ Also, $f(x)$ has a vertical asymptote at $x=3.$ The root and asymptote divide the number line into three subintervals:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,\\frac{11}{4}),\\,(\\frac{11}{4},3),\\,(3,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,\\frac{11}{4})$ | $(\\frac{11}{4},3)$ | $(3,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $11-4x$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| $3-x$ | $+$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the inequality $f(x)<0,$ we look at the bottom row to find out where $f(x)$ is negative.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)$ is negative on the interval $(\\frac{11}{4},3).$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\nf(x)<0\\,\\text{for all}\\,x\\in (\\,\\frac{11}{4},\\,3).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-324126/field-1" "q-324126/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16253771-4d04-5f82-97ab-830e05f9e15a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-324126"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115810/selection/f90ae0eabb62fec144c0f3d69f0ba80792834bb92d199ad9d5d266be8551ae20" :answer/id #uuid "f9d76c42-b9de-52b9-96b3-4f4ebd131727" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,\\frac{5}{4})\\cup (3,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115810/selection/248948d8951d36e5c0e28118086396d990f674509e55dc786342bc366fe1bdf4" :answer/id #uuid "0a2d026a-614a-54ea-a862-806b4b76d99c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-\\frac{5}{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115810/selection/4cc598f0ee1227aa4e0bfbea1564e45e214ce9036a4dc6a52cee1d1c34d0ce44" :answer/id #uuid "028d5493-4ac9-5b1f-a730-219b156efdea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-\\frac{1}{4})\\cup (3,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115810/selection/d44b77730e9eaf6151fbb2e31510ad6b7ef0e4618881dab8f03927002a1d59c0" :answer/id #uuid "b94d748f-4873-5766-b113-6da9a45bee8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (\\frac{5}{4},\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115810/selection/0177d7fa534c75ff5d338933823b11f4bb862c84b895fc983e34c9f40afb42c7" :answer/id #uuid "6f25ce39-84e1-50dd-b888-8e36ef9e1f48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115810/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f02ca864-5ae2-52d7-bad1-1afeed27ae7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115810/selection/f90ae0eabb62fec144c0f3d69f0ba80792834bb92d199ad9d5d266be8551ae20" :answer-field/choices ["q-115810/selection/f90ae0eabb62fec144c0f3d69f0ba80792834bb92d199ad9d5d266be8551ae20" "q-115810/selection/248948d8951d36e5c0e28118086396d990f674509e55dc786342bc366fe1bdf4" "q-115810/selection/4cc598f0ee1227aa4e0bfbea1564e45e214ce9036a4dc6a52cee1d1c34d0ce44" "q-115810/selection/d44b77730e9eaf6151fbb2e31510ad6b7ef0e4618881dab8f03927002a1d59c0" "q-115810/selection/0177d7fa534c75ff5d338933823b11f4bb862c84b895fc983e34c9f40afb42c7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115810" :question/id #uuid "92a50d04-8f01-5c43-b9b8-1ea4815acd9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-115810" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\frac{3-x}{4x-5}<0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we define the function $f(x)$ as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{3-x}{4x-5}.\n$$\n\nSo we're now solving the inequality $f(x)<0.$\n\nThe solution to the equation $f(x)=0$ is $x=3.$ Also, $f(x)$ has a vertical asymptote at $x=\\frac{5}{4}.$ The root and asymptote divide the number line into $3$ subintervals:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,\\frac{5}{4}),\\,(\\frac{5}{4},3),\\,(3,\\infty )\n$$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of the intervals at the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,\\frac{5}{4})$ | $(\\frac{5}{4},3)$ | $(3,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3-x$ | $+$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| $4x-5$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the inequality $f(x)<0,$ we look at the bottom row to find out where $f(x)$ is negative.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)$ is negative on the intervals $(-\\infty ,\\frac{5}{4})$ and $(3,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $f(x)<0$ for all $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\frac{5}{4})\\cup (3,\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115810/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16253771-4d04-5f82-97ab-830e05f9e15a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115810"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-274415/field-1/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "58d24def-f54c-5763-b95b-fa8e354ab970" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274415/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e3031dae-4c9a-515d-82f4-9ce530867cb4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274415/field-1/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer-field/choices ["q-274415/field-1/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274415/field-2/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "1783fe90-335f-5a13-9cf3-efa4b97766c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274415/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "ecd5668b-1d68-5c41-abfb-08cfddd5e3c2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274415/field-2/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer-field/choices ["q-274415/field-2/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274415/field-3/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer/id #uuid "51aa0942-474e-54ed-b9d0-5e0ebb621e17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274415/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "e6324a24-c52f-5a8d-9072-cbd492962d4a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274415/field-3/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer-field/choices ["q-274415/field-3/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274415" :question/id #uuid "2096393e-b75e-5b5f-b5b8-180daf222b29" :question/math-academy-id "q-274415" :question/problem "The values of $x$ that satisfy the inequality $\\frac{2x-3}{3x-2}\\ge 0$ lie in the interval\n\n$\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,$\n{{field-1}}\n$)⋃[$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,$\n{{field-3}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we define the function $f(x)$ as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{2x-3}{3x-2}.\n$$\n\nSo we're now solving the inequality $f(x)\\ge 0.$\n\nThe solution to the equation $f(x)=0$ is $x=\\frac{3}{2}.$ Also, $f(x)$ has a vertical asymptote at $x=\\frac{2}{3}.$ The root and asymptote divide the number line into three subintervals:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,\\frac{2}{3}),\\,(\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{3}{2}),\\,(\\frac{3}{2},\\infty )\n$$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,\\frac{2}{3})$ | $(\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{3}{2})$ | $(\\frac{3}{2},\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2x-3$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $3x-2$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the inequality $f(x)\\ge 0,$ we look at the bottom row to find out where $f(x)$ is nonnegative.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)$ is positive on the intervals $(-\\infty ,\\frac{2}{3})$ and $(\\frac{3}{2},\\infty ).$ Since the function equals zero at $x=\\frac{3}{2},$ we include this endpoint in the solution.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nf(x)\\ge 0\\,\\text{for all}\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\,)⋃[\\,\\frac{3}{2},\\,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-274415/field-1" "q-274415/field-2" "q-274415/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16253771-4d04-5f82-97ab-830e05f9e15a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-274415"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-88655/selection/6fce0ef044cdc2592c6c4d841eb50c364dfede351acb1f6b776ddac80d33ad9b" :answer/id #uuid "fd27ff4e-a044-56de-a6da-b89a9a4fc545" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-1,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88655/selection/06e78330d1bb1ec81664c0688a479159d7653f1d36eda8369a9b2752ee5b2015" :answer/id #uuid "3e33e25f-8199-5fd5-acbb-8ac6d19a4007" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-3,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88655/selection/cb2db2c3536d80ef3e6a23ca4b9c540c483fed8d8b3b89ae1e3d882a398517e3" :answer/id #uuid "0dc3aaee-25d5-5fce-b602-71389f5cf746" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88655/selection/0177d7fa534c75ff5d338933823b11f4bb862c84b895fc983e34c9f40afb42c7" :answer/id #uuid "b6ecc5b6-942f-5ddd-8f29-6ed6fde45c84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88655/selection/978039fa9c1dd18d9ec26cf8af72ef85479108887e604bfc82c338803a703ade" :answer/id #uuid "77573b66-721d-513f-86a3-eca42f55b6d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-1,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88655/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "be23d0c1-a774-57d9-8525-1040c8034b4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-88655/selection/6fce0ef044cdc2592c6c4d841eb50c364dfede351acb1f6b776ddac80d33ad9b" :answer-field/choices ["q-88655/selection/6fce0ef044cdc2592c6c4d841eb50c364dfede351acb1f6b776ddac80d33ad9b" "q-88655/selection/06e78330d1bb1ec81664c0688a479159d7653f1d36eda8369a9b2752ee5b2015" "q-88655/selection/cb2db2c3536d80ef3e6a23ca4b9c540c483fed8d8b3b89ae1e3d882a398517e3" "q-88655/selection/0177d7fa534c75ff5d338933823b11f4bb862c84b895fc983e34c9f40afb42c7" "q-88655/selection/978039fa9c1dd18d9ec26cf8af72ef85479108887e604bfc82c338803a703ade"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-88655" :question/id #uuid "b0d0f9ac-c31b-5cb0-a5b9-34f876646895" :question/math-academy-id "q-88655" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\frac{x-3}{x+1}<0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we define the function $f(x)$ as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{x-3}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nSo we're now solving the inequality $f(x)<0.$\n\nThe solution to the equation $f(x)=0$ is $x=3.$ Also, $f(x)$ has a vertical asymptote at $x=-1.$ The root and asymptote divide the number line into $3$ subintervals:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,-1),\\,(-1,3),\\,(3,\\infty )\n$$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of the intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-1)$ | $(-1,3)$ | $(3,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x-3$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $x+1$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the inequality $f(x)<0,$ we look at the bottom row to find out where $f(x)$ is negative.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)$ is negative on the interval $(-1,3).$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $f(x)<0$ for all $x\\in (-1,3).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-88655/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16253771-4d04-5f82-97ab-830e05f9e15a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-88655"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-88656/selection/c9619f196db109db357741bcab6f0253ab6160ea8726443e7b118d72e6cbe74c" :answer/id #uuid "46af4fb2-f2f6-539e-ad6f-251f02d33746" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in [-2,-\\frac{1}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88656/selection/d3bc2e07ba978d8b0d63af39128d76cf52143ce0439aa58b2abfbaaba34d075d" :answer/id #uuid "6574c863-9d14-5c58-8847-7be053c9955f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-2]\\cup (-\\frac{1}{2},\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88656/selection/2bf16797bec59b3af06d8c744e77f646a8de7155d4e87a83e0e4a297383761f1" :answer/id #uuid "43ee87a2-9efe-5eef-8084-25bcfbf7731a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-2]\\cup [\\frac{1}{2},\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88656/selection/6045830b9e9f49ef053dc03b3608bc02cbc21af2b3e8dd6f0e71690b8c032a9f" :answer/id #uuid "801f6367-49cd-513c-9bd3-5a46aeca454d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in [-2,-\\frac{1}{2}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88656/selection/6b06b159af49b5be6c9ed307531ab3235da995ebd8c92e29e169933209bfa45a" :answer/id #uuid "72f9c464-e920-5b73-bd8c-082ab168c4b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in [\\frac{1}{2},2]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88656/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6b84b5f6-7f3f-584e-92c7-c52bd38020f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-88656/selection/c9619f196db109db357741bcab6f0253ab6160ea8726443e7b118d72e6cbe74c" :answer-field/choices ["q-88656/selection/c9619f196db109db357741bcab6f0253ab6160ea8726443e7b118d72e6cbe74c" "q-88656/selection/d3bc2e07ba978d8b0d63af39128d76cf52143ce0439aa58b2abfbaaba34d075d" "q-88656/selection/2bf16797bec59b3af06d8c744e77f646a8de7155d4e87a83e0e4a297383761f1" "q-88656/selection/6045830b9e9f49ef053dc03b3608bc02cbc21af2b3e8dd6f0e71690b8c032a9f" "q-88656/selection/6b06b159af49b5be6c9ed307531ab3235da995ebd8c92e29e169933209bfa45a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-88656" :question/id #uuid "8b338aae-74fc-5d1d-9908-3c10cfcf64bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-88656" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\frac{x+2}{2x+1}\\le 0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we define the function $f(x)$ as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{x+2}{2x+1}.\n$$\n\nSo we're now solving the inequality $f(x)\\le 0.$\n\nThe solution to the equation $f(x)=0$ is $x=-2.$ Also, $f(x)$ has a vertical asymptote at $x=-\\frac{1}{2}.$  The root and asymptote divide the number line into $3$ subintervals:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,-2),\\,(-2,-\\frac{1}{2}),\\,(-\\frac{1}{2},\\infty )\n$$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of the intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-2)$ | $(-2,-\\frac{1}{2})$ | $(-\\frac{1}{2},\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+2$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $2x+1$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the inequality $f(x)\\le 0,$ we look at the bottom row to find out where $f(x)$ is negative.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)$ is negative on the interval $(-2,-\\frac{1}{2}).$\n\nTherefore, remembering that the root of $f(x)$ is also a solution, we conclude that $f(x)\\le 0$ for all $x\\in [-2,-\\frac{1}{2}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-88656/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16253771-4d04-5f82-97ab-830e05f9e15a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-88656"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-88711/selection/d6d03c73ad8ac8c08c45a3c0b7c1ba1d67e7c19c6024698bd21db264b3b8eb17" :answer/id #uuid "791360d6-5492-5c4f-ad3e-609cccd67db8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-4,-1)\\cup (-\\frac{1}{2},\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88711/selection/c701679c95dc7c22cdc5d611bb9a967ef1d00b9de4c999f213d883c5e665ddbd" :answer/id #uuid "0f2fe62a-2878-5e4